{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01DUEmgYPRd2EQ8AbDTMVgsQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote `ai-engineering/answers/04-002-what-is-peftlora-and-when-use-it.md` covering:\n\n**What is PEFT/LoRA and when use it?**\n\n- **Concept** — PEFT trains only 0.1–2% of parameters (new weight deltas) while freezing the base model; LoRA specifically injects two low-rank matrices (B×A, rank r) per attention layer\n- **Mechanism** — `W_effective = W_frozen + (α/r)·B·A`; detailed hyperparameter guide (rank 4–64, α = 2×r, target modules, LR); full PEFT taxonomy table (LoRA, QLoRA, Prefix Tuning, Adapters, IA³)\n- **VRAM math** — 7B model full fine-tune requires 40+ GB (optimizer states); LoRA rank=16 adds ~200 MB, fits in a single A100 40GB\n- **Example** — Llama 3 8B code-review assistant: 8K training pairs, 4h on 1×A100, ROUGE-L 0.71→0.84, cost $0.002/review vs $0.04 GPT-4o\n- **Decision tree** — full FT (>40GB, >100K data) → LoRA (16–40GB) → QLoRA (<16GB/consumer GPU)\n- **Pitfalls** — confusing \"adding layers\" with frozen-base low-rank delta; not knowing rank/alpha values; not distinguishing LoRA from QLoRA"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":67832,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":297,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91a9730d-6927-4ae5-9c70-97167735b616","uuid":"ea5a4b52-5813-49d7-91df-b386a9268836"}
